// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #5958 new: Browser External Extensions Silent Install Detection (Windows, macOS, Linux)
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/5958
// Pull request author: Fz0x00
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Suspicious Browser External Extension File Creation on Linux
// Sigma ID: 705caf61-b5ef-4b70-b9f9-5708eb0ee14d
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: PersonalRules
// Date: 2026-04-23 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, T1176.001
// Description: Detects the creation of External Extensions JSON files in browser-specific directories on Linux.
//   External extensions can be installed from external update URLs or local CRX files without user
//   interaction. Supported by Chrome, Chromium, and Edge. Adversaries may abuse this to silently
//   install malicious browser extensions.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate software installers registering browser extensions
//   - Package managers installing browser extension packages
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/extensions/developer-guide/alternate-distribution-options
//   - https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/chrome/common/chrome_paths.cc
//   - https://github.com/praetorian-inc/ChromeAlone
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/52dd384fb832f0cd09cb37b9b122f029f9168a9b/rules/linux/file_event/file_event_lnx_browser_external_extension.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath contains "/usr/share/google-chrome/extensions/" or FolderPath contains "/.config/google-chrome/External Extensions/" or FolderPath contains "/usr/share/chromium/extensions/" or FolderPath contains "/.config/chromium/External Extensions/" or FolderPath contains "/usr/share/microsoft-edge/extensions/" or FolderPath contains "/.config/microsoft-edge/External Extensions/"
